## 3. FORMAL SYSTEM DEFINITION

**Definition 3.1 (PCMDHA Hand System).** The complete PCMDHA dexterous hand system is the seven-tuple

$$\mathcal{H} = (S_m,\; A_e,\; C_p,\; \Phi,\; \Theta,\; \mathcal{G}_{\text{kin}},\; \mathcal{P}_{\text{grasp}})$$

where:

- $S_m = \{M_i\}_{i=1}^{N_s}$ — hollow composite skeletal modules, each occupying domain $\Omega_i \subset \mathbb{R}^3$ with anisotropic stiffness $\mathbf{C}^{(i)}$ and density $\rho_i(\mathbf{x})$;
- $A_e = \{(\text{coil}_j, \text{magnet}_j, \text{gap}_j)\}_{j=1}^{N_a}$ — distributed actuators, each a micro-coil plus NdFeB Halbach source;
- $C_p = \{\text{wg}_l, \text{src}_l, \text{det}_l\}_{l=1}^{N_p}$ — photonic channels, each a PDMS polymer waveguide with source-detector pair;
- $\Phi: S_m \times A_e \to \mathbb{R}^3$ — field-coupling map returning the magnetic flux density at each structural node;
- $\Theta: C_p \times S_m \to \mathbb{R}^{N_p}$ — photonic readout map from waveguide deformations to differential optical intensities;
- $\mathcal{G}_{\text{kin}}$ — the kinematic graph of Definition 2.1;
- $\mathcal{P}_{\text{grasp}}$ — the grasp contact topology map assigning contact normals and friction cones at fingertip surfaces.

**Definition 3.2 (Admissible State Space).** The admissible state space of $\mathcal{H}$ is

$$X_{\mathcal{H}} = \left\{ (\mathbf{u}, \mathbf{B}_{\text{field}}, \mathbf{I}_{\text{opt}}, \mathbf{q}) \in H^1(\Omega) \times L^2(\Omega; \mathbb{R}^3) \times \mathbb{R}^{N_p} \times \mathbb{R}^{N_{\text{DOF}}} \;\middle|\right.$$
$$\sigma_{ij}(\mathbf{u})n_j = f_i^{\text{surface}} \text{ on } \partial\Omega_N,\quad \mathbf{u} = 0 \text{ on } \partial\Omega_D,$$
$$\nabla \cdot \mathbf{B}_{\text{field}} = 0,\quad |\mathbf{B}_{\text{field}}| \leq B_{\text{sat}},$$
$$I_{\text{opt},k} \geq I_{\text{noise}} \;\forall k,\quad \mathbf{q} \in \mathcal{Q}_{\text{finger}}\Bigg\}$$

where $\mathcal{Q}_{\text{finger}}$ is the joint angle polytope encoding anatomically-feasible finger configurations:

$$\mathcal{Q}_{\text{finger}} = \left\{ \mathbf{q} \in \mathbb{R}^{27} \;\middle|\; q_j^{\min} \leq q_j \leq q_j^{\max} \;\forall j,\quad \mathbf{A}_{\text{couple}} \mathbf{q} \leq \mathbf{b}_{\text{couple}} \right\}$$

The coupling constraint $\mathbf{A}_{\text{couple}} \mathbf{q} \leq \mathbf{b}_{\text{couple}}$ encodes the DIP-PIP anatomical coupling: $q_{\text{DIP},i} \leq 0.67 \, q_{\text{PIP},i}$ for fingers II–V.

