### 6.3 Thermal Constraint and Active Electromagnetic Damping

Joule heating power: $P_J = I^2 R_c$.

Steady-state temperature rise with natural convection (convection coefficient $h_c \approx 10$ W m⁻² K⁻¹):

$$\Delta T = \frac{I^2 R_c}{h_c A_{\text{surf}}}$$

Back-EMF under joint motion at angular velocity $\dot{q}$:

$$\mathcal{E}_{\text{back}} = -k_F \dot{s} = -k_F r \dot{q}$$

Active damping force when coil is connected to damping resistor $R_d$:

$$F_d = -\frac{k_F^2}{R_c + R_d} \dot{s} = -c_{\text{em}} \dot{s}$$

Effective electromagnetic damping coefficient:

$$c_{\text{em}} = \frac{(2NwB_0)^2}{R_c + R_d} = \frac{k_F^2}{R_c + R_d}$$

The H-bridge switching circuit transitions between current-source actuation and resistive damping within sub-millisecond transition time.

